# Copy to cfg-universe.env in the universe directory. Do not commit it.
# It is read, never executed, by the base's own reader (base/deploy/settings.sh,
# univ-minimal INTENT.md#settings): blank lines, # comments and KEY=value lines of
# the base's parameters only — an unknown key, a key given twice, a secret value or
# shell syntax ($, backquotes, ;, |, a second word) is refused before anything runs.
# It is the one settings file of the universe: deploy/podman-up.sh, deploy/proof.sh
# and deploy/base.sh read it, then hand it to the base's scripts in ENV_FILE
# (base/cfg-univ-minimal.env is also a link to it, for a base script run on its own).
# Every value is an instance parameter (Rule 0B); nothing here is a secret, and no
# secret has a default.

# The instance slug: the manifest's "universe", the same name. Each base unit runs
# as <universe>-ctr-<slug> (vault, logger, queue, maestro).
SHAPER_UNIVERSE=univ-example

# Where each unit's Turbinobash layout lives inside the universe container:
# <root>/<slug>/etc/mysql (its password), etc/identity (its bootstrap and the pin),
# sav (its datadir and dumps) and log where it declares one.
SHAPER_APPS_ROOT=/apps

# Leave both empty and pin cfg-image-lock.json (TEST and PROD), or name the machine's
# registry and a tag the unit images were published under (DEV). DEV only:
# SHAPER_REGISTRY=localhost names images built on this machine with SHAPER_PUSH=0.
# A published tag is never moved: a new build gets a new tag.
SHAPER_REGISTRY=
SHAPER_IMAGE_TAG=

# The universe identity, a lowercase UUID. Leave it empty: the base generates it
# once, beside the Vault master key (<root>/vault/etc/vault/universe-id), and
# refuses a value that differs from the one recorded. Named here only to re-create
# a universe whose identity is known; it is not a secret.
SHAPER_UNIVERSE_ID=

# Where the proof keeps its state and its own reader identity (root-only).
# PROOF_STATE_DIR=/var/lib/univ-proof/univ-example

# The base's secrets store (univ-minimal INTENT.md#secret-files): root-only,
# one directory per consumer; each secret a unit consumes reaches it as its own
# read-only file, named by <NAME>_FILE. A universe with units of its own names its
# universe-wide store here (<universe>/.state/secrets), shared with its units, the
# same layout. No secret value ever goes in this file: the base refuses a secret
# given a value (VAULT_TOKEN=…, *_PASSWORD=…).
# SHAPER_SECRETS_ROOT=/apps/.state/secrets
